how can i make the mainimage from a base directory that is filled with .lzm files and include its modules/root?
Apr 24

The .lzm files are DSL/Knoppix compressed loop modules — squashfs-based. You need to extract them all, merge into a unified root, then repack as the KNOPPIX image.

Full workflow:
bash

# 1. Create working dirs
mkdir -p /home/qemu/extract /home/qemu/merged

# 2. Mount and extract each .lzm
for lzm in /path/to/base/*.lzm; do
    name=$(basename $lzm .lzm)
    mkdir -p /mnt/lzm_$name
    mount -t squashfs $lzm /mnt/lzm_$name -o loop,ro
    cp -ax /mnt/lzm_$name/. /home/qemu/merged/
    umount /mnt/lzm_$name
done

3. Include modules and root directories:
bash

# If your base dir has modules/ and root/ subdirs
cp -ax /path/to/base/modules/. /home/qemu/merged/
cp -ax /path/to/base/root/.    /home/qemu/merged/root/

4. Repack merged tree into KNOPPIX image:
bash

# mksquashfs with DSL-compatible options
mksquashfs /home/qemu/merged /home/qemu/KNOPPIX \
    -b 65536 \
    -comp zlib \
    -no-progress \
    -noappend

5. Verify:
bash

file /home/qemu/KNOPPIX
# Should say: Squashfs filesystem, little endian...

mkdir -p /mnt/verify
mount -t squashfs /home/qemu/KNOPPIX /mnt/verify -o loop,ro
ls /mnt/verify/bin /mnt/verify/lib /mnt/verify/etc
umount /mnt/verify

6. Place into maindrive structure:
bash

# Mount maindrive
mkdir -p /mnt/maindrive
mount -t ext2 /home/qemu/maindrive.img /mnt/maindrive -o loop

mkdir -p /mnt/maindrive/KNOPPIX
cp /home/qemu/KNOPPIX /mnt/maindrive/KNOPPIX/KNOPPIX

umount /mnt/maindrive

Key points:

    -b 65536 matches DSL's native block size
    -comp zlib for compatibility with DSL's older squashfs tools — do not use xz or lz4
    Layer order matters in the for loop — later .lzm files overwrite earlier ones, so put base system first, modules last
    root/ contents typically go to /home/qemu/merged/root/ which becomes the default user homedir inside DSL

What does your base directory structure look like? Paste ls output and I can tailor the merge order.

